// ── Session 2026-03-14k additions ─────────────────────────────────────────────

D072|graph-first-response-vigilance|defined|G-MP1 architecture: inhibition happens before output in the graph layer (not after via evaluator LLM). predict_next() + gradient_flatness() on generation graph injected into _build_think_context() as [REFLEXIVE_PATTERN]. LLM self-inhibits obvious path. Cost=microseconds. Gate=IGOR_NPASS_REPLY. Biology basis: ART vigilance gate + attractor dynamics + Global Workspace Theory. TWM IS the narrative engine activation state — not two things. FLATNESS DIRECTION: gradient_flatness()=0.0 means STEEP (strong dominant prediction = REFLEXIVE); =1.0 means FLAT (no dominant prediction = novel/uncertain). LOW flatness = reflexive = inject warning. HIGH flatness = no graph data = D073 escalation signal.
D073|llm-escalation-is-graph-exhaustion|defined|We reach up to LLM only when graph traversal has genuinely exhausted — enough real time + passes + resonance cycles to honestly say "I don't know." Not a canned fallback. flatness() that never converges (stays LOW after many cycles) = genuinely stuck = escalate. Contrast: flatness HIGH immediately = reflexive = inhibit and re-traverse (D072). Factual queries: achievable soon. Fuzzy/generative queries: harder, deferred. Principle: "the program is the data" — the graph IS the knowledge; LLM is the trainer, not the primary answerer.

