D196|surface-habit-inhibition-substrate|decided|Most memories carry only a 'surface' habit because surfacing deposits a candidate into TWM without acting — inhibitory forces (BG threshold scoring, milieu gates, arousal weighting) then decide whether the content fires. This is correct: cognition's job is to inhibit, not to generate. Direct-action habits bypass inhibition and are wrong for general memory retrieval. Part of memory definition.
D196|surface-habit-inhibition-substrate|decided|Memories default to surface habit — deposits TWM candidate without acting; inhibitory forces (BG/milieu/arousal) decide if it fires. Cognition's job is inhibition not generation. Part of memory definition.
