D220|instance-memory-scope-spec|defined|Ticket #123 design spec: scope column (class/instance/session) on memories table, single table not split. Migration: CORE_PATTERN/IDENTITY/PROCEDURAL/INTERPRETIVE → class; EPISODIC/TWM → instance. igor_instance_id FK null for class-scope. Prereq: confirm IgorInstance model exists before worker-ready.
D221|no-row-scans|decided|All memory access is graph traversal from hot nodes, never row scans. No query should ask 'give me all memories of type X' — that pattern is non-biological and doesn't scale. Every query starts from an already-warm node (hot_attractors, TWM, trail heat) and traverses edges. Corollary: collections (employer journal, etc.) are subtrees rooted at a node, not flat lists. Interim: SQL queries scoped by activation threshold. Real fix: read from live hot_attractor state.
D222|llm-tool-dispatch|decided|LLM tiers must be able to dispatch tools directly, not just narrate them. Current: tools only fire via PROCEDURAL habit code_ref. Gap: LLM generates prose describing tool calls but never executes them. Fix: extend two-phase response pipeline to parse <tool>name</tool><tool_args>{json}</tool_args> blocks from LLM output, look up in registry, execute, inject result into ring. System prompt teaches the format. This makes every registered tool available to any LLM tier — not just habits. Habit dispatch remains the fast path; LLM dispatch is the fallback for novel/uncovered cases.
