D290|engram-label-instruction|defined|LABEL instruction: no-op marker in payload cell. ['LABEL', '@name']. BRANCHIF target starting with '@' = local label; bare string = memory node ID. Executor loop must be index-based to support backward jumps.
D291|engram-stopif-instruction|defined|STOPIF instruction: ['STOPIF', condition]. Conditional terminator. IF x STOP. Complements ENDIF (unconditional stop). Simpler than BRANCHIF-to-nowhere.
D292|engram-branch-trigger|defined|Reserved trigger '__entry__' fires on every branch arrival at a node. Original trigger already in trail (inspectable). Additional trigger cells on target node may also fire on top of __entry__.
D293|engram-fork-async|defined|FORKIF spawns async background jobs — not inline. Biology wouldn't do it synchronously.
D294|engram-loop-detection|defined|Loop termination: track {node_id: basket_snapshot} per traversal. On arrival: if node seen before AND basket unchanged since last visit → stop. Basket mutation = progress, continue. Identical basket = infinite loop, exit.
D295|engram-memory-channel|defined|EmitChannel 'memory': deposits a new memory node. key=memory_type (EPISODIC/PROCEDURAL/etc.), value=content string. Extra metadata from basket: _mem_tags (list), _mem_identity_weight (float, default 0.5), _mem_salience (float, default 0.5). Requires _cortex in basket.
D296|engram-branchif-trigger-target|defined|BRANCHIF target syntax: 'node_id#trigger_name' invokes a specific cell on the target node. Hash separator. Bare node_id still uses __entry__ as default. Enables if/else/loop patterns — same node, different arrival cells. ExecutionResult gains next_trigger field.
D297|layer3-cognitive-stdlib|defined|Layer 3 cognitive standard library: 8 foundational bricks (PARSE_GOAL, SITUATE, DECOMPOSE, ANTICIPATE, CONSTRAIN, OBSERVE, REPLAN, SCOPE_CHECK). Planning = chaining these. Confidence threading runs through all. Re-entrant by design — planning recurs after every step, not front-loaded. Foundation for coding/planning engrams.
D297|layer3-cognitive-stdlib|defined|Layer 3 cognitive standard library: 9 foundational bricks (PARSE_GOAL, SITUATE, DECOMPOSE, ANTICIPATE, CONSTRAIN, OBSERVE, HYPOTHESIZE, REPLAN, SCOPE_CHECK). Planning = chaining these. Confidence threading runs through all. Re-entrant by design. HYPOTHESIZE = abductive reasoning from delta — how might that work? Foundation for coding/planning engrams.
D298|hypothesize-universal-primitive|defined|HYPOTHESIZE is the universal cognitive primitive. ANTICIPATE = HYPOTHESIZE(forward, goal). Debug hypothesize = HYPOTHESIZE(backward, delta). OBSERVE = prediction error signal. Same loop at every level. ANTICIPATE collapses into HYPOTHESIZE with time_direction basket key (forward/backward). Mirrors D279 predictive coding at layer 3 — brain does not distinguish predicting from explaining. One primitive, two temporal orientations.
D299|forkif-null-target-safe|defined|FORKIF skips targets that are None, falsy, or the string 'None'. Makes optional next_node slot safe in TEMPLATE expansion — Jinja2 renders None slot as 'None' string; node_executor now drops it silently instead of spawning a bad node.
D300|twm-as-inter-subsystem-channel|defined|TWM is the interface channel between cognitive subsystems. Each planning brick writes its durable output to TWM (not just basket); the next brick fires reactively when it observes its precondition in TWM. Basket = within-node scratch space (ephemeral, local). TWM = inter-step pipe (observable, persistent across turns, triggers downstream habits). This is emit+react applied to multi-step planning — not a call chain, not a basket pipeline.
D301|twm-trigger-dispatch-heartbeat|done|HeartbeatSource._check_twm_trigger_habits: scan for twm_trigger metadata, push proactive ACTION_IMPULSE when TWM category matches
D302|cascade-management-phrases|done|MANAGEMENT_PHRASES for coding cascade tools — adopt top ticket, goal continuation, coding sprint, close goal, read active goal bypass BG to direct code_ref dispatch
D303|cascade-end-to-end-bugs-fixed|done|Three bugs blocked D301 cascade: (1) get_procedural_by_metadata_key used SQLite json_extract on PG — fixed to jsonb_exists(); (2) _check_twm_trigger_habits used twm_read(limit=5 ASC) — GOAL_READY buried under reading entries, fixed to category-filtered direct query; (3) ACTION_IMPULSE buried under 50 non-integrated READING_STEW in drain queue — fixed to call code_ref directly. run_coding_sprint also needed ACTIVE_GOAL fallback (2h TTL expires before sprint fires).
D304|slates-are-dailies|defined|Slates are daily work files at ~/.TheIgors/claudecode/YYYYMMDD.slate.txt — one per day, no numbering, no topic sections. Epics are permanent category tags on tickets. History is in dated files; queue is truth for what's pending.
